\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two gradings for two kinds of generators}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{An operator [odd in cell degree](fdip-00UD) joins cells of
opposite parity. In each term of its bilinear one generator
acquires the unit and the other its inverse. By
\ref{fdip-014A}, a Ginsparg–Wilson operator sends each eigenspace
of its modified grading into the opposite eigenspace of its
original grading. Every generator occurs once in the top word.
Which grading acts on each kind of generator, and what factor
does the top word acquire?}
